  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partners Capacity Strengthening Support 2018-2021</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2018 CAFOD Sierra Leone undertook an organisational assessment of five partners through which areas to develop/improved were identified. This will improve programme quality and organisational structure if implemented correctly. The five partners: KADDRO, Street Child of Sierra Leone, Justice and Peace Commission Kenema, Missionary Sisters of the Holy Rosery and Handmaid Sisters Pendembu have developed a three-year plan from 2018-2021 based on key priority areas. This work is aimed at improving project management, execution and organisational capacity.

In the second phase of this project, additional partners were added into the project whilst inactive partners were excluded. The second phase began with an update from KADDRO, Missionary Sisters of the Holy Rosary and Handmaid Sisters of Pendembu on the progress made against their three-year plans. CAFOD Sierra Leone has also added Caritas Kenema (which is undergoing restructuring and receiving organisational support from CAFOD) and the Inter-Religious Council of Sierra Leone.</narrative>
  </description>
